<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Labib al-Amiri</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">11th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Labib al-Amiri was a slav freedman of the Amirid household who seized <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tortosa">Tortosa</a> after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">Caliphate</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cordoba">Córdoba</a> collapsed in civil war in 1009, founding the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taifa">taifa</a> of Tortosa. He is reported to have shared for a time in the government of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valencia">Valencia</a> with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/freedmen">freedmen</a> Mubarak and Muzaffar. Tortosa's independence ended when it was annexed by the taifa of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zaragoza">Zaragoza</a>.</p></div>
